&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;GitLab is the intelligent orchestration platform for DevSecOps. GitLab enables organizations to increase developer productivity, improve operational efficiency, reduce security and compliance risk, and accelerate digital transformation. More than 50 million registered users and more than 50% of the Fortune 100* trust GitLab to ship better, more secure software faster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The same principles built into our products are reflected in how our team works: we embrace AI as a core productivity multiplier, with all team members expected to incorporate AI into their daily workflows to drive efficiency, innovation, and impact. GitLab is where careers accelerate, innovation flourishes, and every voice is valued. Our high-performance culture is driven by our values&amp;nbsp;and continuous knowledge exchange, enabling our team members to reach their full potential while collaborating with industry leaders to solve complex problems. &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=OuZIb5zszQI&quot;&gt;Co-create the future with us&lt;/a&gt; as we build technology that transforms how the world develops software.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;*&lt;em&gt;Fortune 500® is a registered trademark of Fortune Media IP Limited, used under license. Claim based on GitLab data. Fortune 100 refers to the top 20% ranked companies in the 2025 Fortune 500 list, published in June 2025. Fortune and Fortune Media IP Limited are not affiliated with, and do not endorse products or services of GitLab.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;An overview of this role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a Strategic Account Executive for Singapore, you will own and grow GitLab’s enterprise relationships in the Singapore market. You’ll help large organizations realize the full value of GitLab’s AI-powered DevSecOps platform by leading the entire sales cycle, from prospecting and qualification through rollout and long-term adoption. Reporting to an Area Sales Manager or Regional Director, you’ll use a consultative approach to understand complex customer needs, guide them through evaluation, and coordinate pre- and post-sales resources to ensure successful deployments and visible business outcomes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’ll work under minimal supervision on complex deals, act as the voice of the customer into GitLab, and partner closely with our strategic channel partners to generate qualified opportunities and develop new customers. In your first year, you’ll be expected to establish and execute clear account plans for enterprise prospects and customers in the Singapore market, build strong internal and external stakeholder relationships, and consistently manage your forecast and pipeline with transparency and discipline.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll do&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support GitLab’s strategic prospects and customers in the Singapore Market, owning the full sales cycle for large and enterprise accounts&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead account strategy by developing and executing account plans aligned to each customer’s business needs and long-term goals&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Conduct prospecting and opportunity development activities in named large and strategic accounts, including working closely with strategic channel partners to generate qualified leads and new customers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate pre- and post-sales engagement with solutions architects, customer success, and support teams to ensure successful rollout, adoption, and expansion of GitLab products&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide clear account leadership, including regular activity, pipeline, and forecast reporting to sales management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze wins and losses, contribute to root cause analysis, and share lessons learned with account managers, marketing, and technical teams to improve future outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the voice of the customer by sharing feedback and product ideas through GitLab’s public issue tracker and internal channels&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Use a consultative sales approach to uncover business issues, shape solution recommendations, and deliver compelling proposals, quotes, and presentations that address customer requirements&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What you’ll bring&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience managing complex sales cycles with large, strategic enterprise customers.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proven ability to prospect, qualify, and develop new opportunities while also growing existing accounts through strong account management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Skill in leading pre- and post-sales activities, coordinating with technical, support, and channel partners to drive adoption and expansion&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency in consultative selling, including uncovering business needs, building account plans, and delivering proposals and presentations that align GitLab solutions to customer outcomes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ability to prepare and maintain accurate activity, pipeline, and forecast reports, and to contribute to win/loss and root cause analysis&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Effective communication and collaboration skills to share customer feedback and lessons learned with sales management, product, marketing, and technical teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with software development concepts and tools, with preferred exposure to Git, software development tools, or application lifecycle management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Alignment with GitLab’s values, openness to learning, and interest in applying transferable skills even if your background does not match every requirement exactly&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the team&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;The Strategic Account Executive will join our enterprise sales team, which focuses on driving GitLab adoption with large customers in the Singapore market. The team is responsible for the full relationship lifecycle with enterprise accounts, from initial engagement through long-term expansion and advocacy, ensuring customers realize value from GitLab’s DevSecOps platform. Team members work in an all-remote, distributed environment and collaborate asynchronously across time zones with sales leadership, solutions architects, customer success, marketing, and channel partners. The team is currently focused on maintaining and growing our existing footprint in the region, executing a consistent global sales motion while adapting to local customer needs and partnering closely with strategic channel organizations to reach and support key accounts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;h4&gt;&lt;strong&gt;How GitLab Supports Full-Time Employees&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/benefits/general-and-entity-benefits/&quot;&gt;Benefits to support your health, finances, and well-being&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/people-group/time-off-and-absence/time-off-types/#flexible-paid-time-off-pto&quot;&gt;Flexible Paid Time Off&amp;nbsp;&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/company/culture/inclusion/tmrg-tmag/&quot;&gt;Team Member Resource Groups&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/stock-options/&quot;&gt;Equity Compensation &amp;amp; Employee Stock Purchase Plan&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/people-group/learning-and-development/growth-and-development/&quot;&gt;Growth and Development Fund&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/total-rewards/benefits/general-and-entity-benefits/#parental-leave&quot;&gt;Parental Leave&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Please note that we welcome interest from candidates with varying levels of experience; many successful candidates do not meet every single requirement. Additionally, studies have shown that people from &lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/company/culture/inclusion/#examples-of-select-underrepresented-groups&quot;&gt;underrepresented groups&lt;/a&gt; are less likely to apply to a job unless they meet every single qualification. If you&#39;re excited about this role, please apply and allow our recruiters to assess your application.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;hr&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Country Hiring Guidelines: &lt;/strong&gt;GitLab hires new team members in countries around the world. All of our roles are remote, however some roles may carry specific location-based eligibility requirements. Our Talent Acquisition team can help answer any questions about location after starting the recruiting process.&amp;nbsp;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Privacy Policy: &lt;/strong&gt;Please review our &lt;a href=&quot;https://handbook.gitlab.com/handbook/hiring/candidate-faq/recruitment-privacy-policy/&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;Recruitment Privacy Policy.&lt;/a&gt; Your privacy is important to us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;GitLab is proud to be an equal opportunity workplace and is an affirmative action employer. GitLab’s policies and practices relating to recruitment, employment, career development and advancement, promotion, and retirement are based solely on merit, regardless of race, color, religion, ancestry, sex (including pregnancy, lactation, sexual orientation, gender identity, or gender expression), national origin, age, citizenship, marital status, mental or physical disability, genetic information (including family medical history), discharge status from the military, protected veteran status (which includes disabled veterans, recently separated veterans, active duty wartime or campaign badge veterans, and Armed Forces service medal veterans), or any other basis protected by law. GitLab will not tolerate discrimination or harassment based on any of these characteristics. See also&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/people-policies/inc-usa/#equal-employment-opportunity-policy&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;GitLab’s EEO Policy&lt;/a&gt;&amp;nbsp;and&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/labor-and-employment-notices/#eeoc-us-equal-employment-opportunity-commission-notices&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;EEO is the Law&lt;/a&gt;. If you have a disability or special need that requires&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/people-policies/inc-usa/#reasonable-accommodation&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;accommodation&lt;/a&gt;, please let us know during the&amp;nbsp;&lt;a href=&quot;https://about.gitlab.com/handbook/hiring/interviewing/#adjustments-to-our-interview-process&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot;&gt;recruiting process&lt;/a&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About CoLab&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;At CoLab, we help mechanical engineering teams bring life-changing products to market years sooner.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We build AI for engineers designing cars, medical devices, and jet engines. Products this complex aren&#39;t sketched and sent to production. Teams spend months on iterations, reviews, and tests, predicting how every part performs before anything is built. CoLab is where those reviews happen, and we capture the rationale behind every change. Other tools show what changed between versions. Only CoLab knows why. That&#39;s how our AI helps manufacturers like Bobcat, Triumph Motorcycles, and GE Appliances make better decisions, eliminate rework cycles, and get to market faster.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Proudly based in St. John’s, Newfoundland, CoLab started with one customer in 2018. Since then we’ve raised a&lt;a href=&quot;https://financialpost.com/pmn/business-wire-news-releases-pmn/ai-is-changing-engineering-colab-just-raised-72m-to-lead-the-transformation&quot;&gt; $72M Series C&lt;/a&gt;, been named the 57th fastest growing company in North America by Deloitte (&lt;a href=&quot;https://financialpost.com/pmn/business-wire-news-releases-pmn/colab-ranked-number-57-fastest-growing-company-in-north-america-on-the-2025-deloitte-technology-fast-500&quot;&gt;Fast 500™&lt;/a&gt;), signed multi-year&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.theglobeandmail.com/business/article-bombardier-signs-contract-colab-ai-software/&quot;&gt; AI partnerships with companies like Bombardier&lt;/a&gt;, and grown to a team of 250+.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About the Role&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a high-impact role that helps define how CoLab delivers technical value to its most strategic customers in Aerospace and Defence. CoLab is a category-creating product, which means adoption isn&#39;t just a rollout. It&#39;s a change in how the organization works.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In this role, you&#39;d act as a trusted advisor, leveraging people, process, and technology to help teams rethink how they manage feedback, data, and decision-making across design and PLM. That means getting deep into customer workflows, testing new ways of working, and building repeatable methods the rest of the team can scale.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You&#39;ll work alongside a Customer Success Manager, and use what you learn on the front line to help shape product direction. This role isn&#39;t about selling or pitching. It&#39;s about deeply understanding engineering problems and solving them alongside the customer.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;We are looking for a candidate in Switzerland to work regularly on-site with local CoLab customers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Our Ideal Candidate&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You’re a mechanical engineer by trade and have worked as a designer in an A&amp;amp;D company. You also understand the full product development life cycle: how design, manufacturing, quality, and engineering leadership depend on each other, and where collaboration breaks down. You can coach those teams toward working together better.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You know how to improve that life cycle with technology. Maybe you’ve championed internal tools or created automation or scripts.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You also know a process that makes sense on paper won’t get adopted on its own. You can meet people where they are, including the stakeholders who don’t want to change.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;You don’t need to be the loudest voice in the room, but you can run a sprint and lead a cross-functional project. If the average person might find this job too undefined or complex, that probably excites you.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Job Responsibilities&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Mapping a customer&#39;s current-state design review and engineering workflows, and defining the target-state process their teams will actually adopt.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Deploying and tuning CoLab&#39;s AI capabilities against a customer&#39;s own standards, drawing checklists, and design guidelines, and diagnosing what&#39;s working and what isn&#39;t.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Providing mechanical engineering expertise to validate AI-generated results and ensure engineering rigor.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Investigating and solving complex engineering data and integration challenges across PLM, ERP, QMS, and traditional design feedback tools.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Expanding adoption into new teams, programs, and sites within the account, partnering with the Customer Success Manager on where the next opportunity sits.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborating with product teams to identify feature gaps, improve capabilities, and refine AutoReview.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Qualifications&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Must-haves:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Background in mechanical design engineering, ideally in a medium- to large-sized organization.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong understanding of PLM &amp;amp; ERP systems and enterprise engineering data architecture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Demonstrated ability to lead technical projects and cross-functional collaborations.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience working directly with customers or internal stakeholders to solve technical problems.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Comfort working in fast-changing, ambiguous environments.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong written communication and documentation skills.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Working knowledge of high-level AI architecture, specifically LLMs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Familiarity with APIs, data integrations, and enterprise architecture concepts.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Located in Switzerland&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Nice-to-haves:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience with internal tool development, scripting, or automation.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Exposure to AI/ML tools applied to engineering workflows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Prior work in design consulting or product development at scale.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Travel Expectations&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;While this is a fully remote role, travel is a consistent part of the job. There are two primary types of travel you can expect:&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Team Weeks:&lt;/strong&gt; Once per quarter, the sales team or entire company gets together in person. These typically involve traveling out on a Monday and returning on a Thursday or Friday. Two of these each year are held at our headquarters in St. John&#39;s, Newfoundland, Canada and the others take place in more central locations that evolve as the team grows.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;On-sites:&lt;/strong&gt; This role will work closely with a local customer with expectations to be on site with that customer, so there will likely be far less travel than our typical MFDE roll. That being said, in the event the local customer were to no longer work with us, the following is our standard MFDE travel expectations: “For most of our large deployment customers, we will visit on-site during kick-off and key expansion opportunities. Most on-sites involve 2-3 days with the customer, with travel on either side. Travel is primarily within North America, and you can expect 4 customer on-sites per quarter.”&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Extra Details&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;This is a full-time, permanent position with a competitive compensation package that includes stock options.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Unlimited paid vacation and extended health benefits&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h2&gt;Equity Note&lt;/h2&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Frequently cited statistics show that people who identify with historically marginalized groups are likely to apply to jobs only if they meet 100% of the qualifications. We encourage you to help us break that statistic and apply even if you don&#39;t meet every single qualification. Your potential is what matters most to us.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.ch">Jobs in Switzerland</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;div class=&quot;content-intro&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Nebius:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nebius is leading a new era in cloud infrastructure for the global AI economy. We are building a full-stack AI cloud platform that supports developers and enterprises from data and model training through to production deployment, without the cost and complexity of building large in-house AI/ML infrastructure.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Built by engineers, for engineers. From large-scale GPU orchestration to inference optimization, we own the hard problems across compute, storage, networking and applied AI.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Listed on Nasdaq (NBIS) and headquartered in Amsterdam, we have a global footprint with R&amp;amp;D hubs across Europe, the UK, North America and Israel. Our team of 1,500+ includes hundreds of engineers with deep expertise across hardware, software and AI R&amp;amp;D.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;h4&gt;The role:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;In Token Factory analytics there is no split into product analysts, ML engineers and data engineers. Each person owns a question end to end: builds the data, runs the analysis, and comes back with a recommendation that changes a decision.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Your responsibilities will include:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Define core product and business metrics and build a single source of truth that Product, Finance, and Sales can rely on.&lt;br&gt;- Build a comprehensive view of self-service customers, including usage patterns, customer health, satisfaction, retention risks, unmet needs, and growth opportunities.&lt;br&gt;- Translate customer demand and commercial plans into capacity forecasts and support capacity allocation decisions.&lt;br&gt;- Measure effective capacity utilization and identify opportunities to improve the commercial value of available capacity.&lt;br&gt;- Develop and evaluate pricing and packaging models, including guaranteed capacity, on-demand pricing, commitments, clawback mechanisms, and provisioned throughput units.&lt;br&gt;- Provide data-driven recommendations for the self-service and managed offerings, including customer segmentation, pricing, and capacity.&lt;br&gt;- Partner with Product, Engineering, Applied AI, Finance, and Sales to turn insights into concrete product and operational improvements.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;We expect you to have:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- 5+ years of experience in analytics or data science.&lt;br&gt;- Strong Python, SQL, and statistics: you understand the code and the methods you use.&lt;br&gt;- Hands-on experience analysing large-scale customer, product, and usage datasets using statistical / analytical or distributed data-processing tools.&lt;br&gt;- AI-assisted coding as your default way of working: you guide it, verify it, and own the result.&lt;br&gt;- The ability to go from a question to a production-ready solution.&lt;br&gt;- The ability to turn complex data into clear recommendations.&lt;br&gt;- Strong commercial and product judgment, with the ability to balance customer value, monetization, growth, and profitability.&lt;br&gt;- Experience with pricing, packaging, monetization, or commercial analytics for technical or consumption-based products.&lt;br&gt;- Strong cross-functional collaboration skills across Product, Engineering, Data, Finance, Sales, and Operations.&lt;br&gt;- A hands-on and proactive working style, with the ability to operate effectively in an ambiguous and technically complex environment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h4&gt;Nice to have:&lt;/h4&gt;
&lt;p&gt;- Familiarity with LLM inference economics: tokens, throughput and latency, batching, GPU costs.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits &amp;amp; Perks:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Competitive compensation&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Career growth and learning opportunities&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Flexibility and ownership&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Collaborative and innovative culture&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Opportunity to work on impactful AI projects&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;International environment and talented teams&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What&#39;s it like to work at Nebius:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Fast moving&amp;nbsp;- Bold thinking&amp;nbsp;- Constant growth&amp;nbsp;- Meaningful impact&amp;nbsp;- Trust and real ownership&amp;nbsp;- Opportunity to shape the future of AI&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Equal Opportunity Statement:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Nebius is an equal opportunity employer. We are committed to fostering an inclusive and diverse workplace and to providing equal employment opportunities in all aspects of employment. We do not discriminate on the basis of race, color, religion, sex (including pregnancy), national origin, ancestry, age, disability, genetic information, marital status, veteran status, sexual orientation, gender identity or expression, or any other characteristic protected by applicable law.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Applicants must be authorized to work in the country in which they apply and will be required to provide proof of employment eligibility as a condition of hire.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;If you need accommodations during the application process, please let us know.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.nl/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in Netherlands</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

